[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/4333/images/headers/10767_1788124839.jpg[/img]

[size=5][b]NATIVE ELDEN RING UI FOR YOUR MOD[/b][/size]

One shared menu host. Multiple client mods. No overlay.

[url=https://github.com/Flammrock/ERNativeUI][b]GITHUB: SOURCE, SDK, DOCUMENTATION AND EXAMPLES[/b][/url]
[url=https://github.com/Flammrock/ERNativeUI/releases/latest]COMPLETE WINDOWS SDK AND RUNTIME RELEASE[/url][/center]

[quote][b]ERNativeUI is primarily an SDK for mod authors.[/b]

It lets a client mod add custom System tabs, native settings, dialogs, title-screen text, text input, color pickers and configurable input bindings without owning another competing set of Elden Ring UI hooks.

[b]Players install one canonical ERNativeUI.dll host.[/b] If a mod lists ERNativeUI as a requirement, download the host from this page's Files tab, install it once, and let every compatible client mod connect to that same copy.[/quote]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/4333/images/10767/10767-1788711733-1600560216.png[/img]
[size=5][b]ERNATIVEUI 1.3.0 / ERUI API 1.3[/b] [sup][color=#d1242f][b][NEW][/b][/color][/sup][/size]

API 1.3 adds native custom System tabs and title-screen status text for client mods.
Existing clients built for APIs 1.0 through 1.2 remain compatible with the 1.3.0 host.[/center]

