[center][size=5][b]MORE THAN CONTROLS[/b][/size][/center]

[b]Menus and pages[/b]
[list]
[*]Add rows to supported built-in Configuration pages: Game Options, Camera Options, Display, Sound, Network, Keyboard/Mouse and Graphics[/*]
[*]Give client mods their own top-level System tabs with independent titles, optional custom icons and ordinary paginated content[/*]
[*]Merge tabs registered by multiple mods, apply optional player ordering and keep overflow reachable through native controller and mouse navigation[/*]
[*]Create client-owned submenus[/*]
[*]Automatic capacity detection and pagination[/*]
[*]Native Next, Previous and Back behavior[/*]
[*]Automatic page numbering and customizable provider-submenu titles[/*]
[/list]

[b]Title-screen text[/b]
[list]
[*]Add short version, status or compatibility lines to any of the four title-screen corners[/*]
[*]Use Elden Ring's native text color or an explicit opaque RGB color[/*]
[*]Adapt placement to the validated live title layout and preserve compatible text already added by other mods[/*]
[*]Requires the default-on runtime GFX completion; disabling runtime patching also disables this capability[/*]
[/list]

[b]Dialogs, localization and configuration[/b]
[list]
[*]Native modal alerts with dismiss-only, one-button or two-button layouts[/*]
[*]Bottom or centered dialog placement[/*]
[*]Runtime detection of Elden Ring's selected Steam language, with an optional host-wide locale override[/*]
[*]Localized ERNativeUI navigation labels with an English fallback[/*]
[*]Provider-owned INI storage and a public input-assignment codec[/*]
[/list]

[b]Player-configurable input bindings[/b]
[list]
[*]Register controller, keyboard and mouse actions[/*]
[*]Show those actions in Elden Ring's native Button Settings and Key Bindings screens[/*]
[*]Receive callbacks when the player activates an action[/*]
[*]Observe assignment and Clear changes so client mods can persist them[/*]
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/4333/images/10767/10767-1788711693-1080782593.png[/img][/center]
[center][size=5][b]FOR PLAYERS: INSTALL THE SHARED HOST ONCE[/b][/size][/center]

[b]Requirements[/b]
[list]
[*]Elden Ring for Windows x64[/*]
[*]The Steam release of Elden Ring[/*]
[*]Mod Engine 2 or another compatible DLL loader[/*]
[*]Offline play with Easy Anti-Cheat disabled[/*]
[*]An ERNativeUI release that explicitly supports the installed Elden Ring executable[/*]
[/list]

[b]1. Download the current file from this page's Files tab.[/b]

[b]2. Extract it as this directory inside your Mod Engine 2 setup:[/b]
[code]mod\ERNativeUI[/code]

[b]3. Add the host before ordinary ERNativeUI client mods in your existing external_dlls list:[/b]
[code][modengine]
external_dlls = [
    "mod\\ERNativeUI\\ERNativeUI.dll",
    "mod\\SomeClientMod\\SomeClientMod.dll"
][/code]

[b]4. Start Elden Ring through Mod Engine 2.[/b]

Only one copy of ERNativeUI.dll should be loaded. The example DLLs included with ERNativeUI are optional demonstrations and are not dependencies for normal client mods.

By default, ERNativeUI completes supported settings GFX in memory while Elden Ring loads it, expanding ordinary settings pages and supplying matching TextInput/ColorPicker presentation without loose ERNativeUI GFX files. Structurally compatible GFX supplied by other mods remains supported; unrecognized layouts are kept unchanged rather than modified speculatively. Players can set [font=Courier New]EnableRuntimePatching = 0[/font] in ERNativeUI.ini's GFX section and restart to leave every effective GFX file untouched; custom tabs and functional widget fallbacks remain available, ERNativeUI adds no rows or presentation, and API 1.3 title-screen text is disabled. Compatible structures already authored into the effective movie remain available.

[font=Courier New]MinimumTabSlots = 8[/font] requests the vanilla minimum and never reduces a compatible movie that already contains more slots. With runtime GFX patching enabled, players may request 8, 9 or 10 physical slots; ten is Elden Ring's hard native ceiling and there is no MaximumTabSlots override. This is separate from logical custom tabs: additional registered tabs remain reachable through ERNativeUI's shifting [font=Courier New]...[/font] viewport. Restart after changing the value.

[url=https://github.com/Flammrock/ERNativeUI/blob/main/docs/getting-started/player-installation.md][b]READ THE COMPLETE PLAYER INSTALLATION GUIDE[/b][/url]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/4333/images/10767/10767-1788711733-1600560216.png[/img][/center]
[center][size=5][b]FOR MOD AUTHORS: BUILD NATIVE UI, NOT ANOTHER OVERLAY[/b][/size][/center]

The complete GitHub Windows package contains the host, public headers, CMake package, built and source examples, licenses and a version-pinned documentation link.

[list]
[*][b]C projects:[/b] include erui.h for the strict C11-compatible ABI.[/*]
[*][b]C++ projects:[/b] include ERNativeUI.hpp for the header-only C++17 wrapper. Keep erui.h beside it when copying the headers because the wrapper includes it internally.[/*]
[*][b]No import library:[/b] client mods negotiate the versioned API table from the host at runtime.[/*]
[*][b]One dependency for players:[/b] declare ERNativeUI as a requirement instead of bundling a private or renamed host copy.[/*]
[/list]

[b]New focused API 1.3 examples:[/b] [url=https://github.com/Flammrock/ERNativeUI/blob/ERNativeUI-v1.3.0/examples/title_screen_text/README.md]Title-Screen Text[/url] demonstrates all four corners and colors. [url=https://github.com/Flammrock/ERNativeUI/blob/ERNativeUI-v1.3.0/examples/custom_tabs_stress/README.md]Custom Tabs Stress[/url] is an intentionally heavy 50-tab integration and performance test, not a template for an ordinary mod.

