[center][size=5][b]COMPATIBILITY AND SUPPORT[/b][/size][/center]

[list]
[*]Use a release that names support for your installed Elden Ring executable after every game update.[/*]
[*]Mod Engine 2 is the primary supported loader.[/*]
[*]ERNativeUI 1.3.0's API 1.3 paths were live-validated on Elden Ring executables 2.7.1.0 and 2.7.2.0. The retained 2.7.0.0 profile supports API 1.0 through 1.2 paths, but build-locked API 1.3 capabilities such as custom tabs are unavailable there.[/*]
[*]Solid Uncapper 2.3 coexistence is verified on Elden Ring 2.7.0.0 and 2.7.1.0 for the exact matrix and scope documented on GitHub; load Solid Uncapper first. It has not been regression-tested with ERNativeUI on 2.7.2.0.[/*]
[*]Seamless Co-op 2.0.1 was live-tested with the Elden Ring 2.7.0.0 reference executable; no incompatibility was observed for that exact combination.[/*]
[*]Shadow of the Erdtree title-screen layout and adaptive spacing were live-tested on Elden Ring 2.7.1.0 with the DLC both absent and present; see the GitHub compatibility matrix for the exact scope.[/*]
[*]Logging is disabled by default and can be enabled in ERNativeUI.ini while troubleshooting.[/*]
[/list]

